+++ b/docs/audits/ROSTER_SOURCE_SCOPE_2249.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Roster source freshness — build 2249
+
+## Confirmed shared defect
+
+Production source `98030d6af189fe7d023bc36251800ab754a24f05` evaluated every canonical catalog projection row when qualifying prepared roster comparisons. A matched native Sleeper fixture added one unrostered missing-projection row: the same 46 rostered players, 174.0 owner optimal points, ten legal starters and +10.0 supported RB addition gain changed from current to provisional. The Market action disappeared. No numerical or availability evidence used by the roster had changed. The original baseline probe and native outputs are retained separately from candidate acceptance.
+
+## Small shared correction
+
+Freshness references all league rostered assets except explicitly stored IR/taxi/reserve or explicitly ineligible rows. Other eligible reserves and other teams remain dependencies of the existing legal lineup and peer reference analysis. This is not a position-specific availability shortcut. In particular, an uncertain K/DEF or FLEX candidate is not promoted to observed participation. A positive projection, roster label or absent injury designation does not prove participation.
+
+All canonical rows still undergo atomic generation compatibility checks. No row is dropped, revalued, filled or relabeled at the source. Post-trade evidence separately qualifies the actual resulting rosters, including assets moved out of storage. Existing read-time aging and failed-refresh qualifications remain effective without a new solver or source request.
+
+## Preserved boundaries
+
+Sleeper is the exclusive fantasy projection/results source. Explicit zeros and negative precision, missing/conflicting facts, account/league/season/scoring isolation, exact picks, neutral/personal pricing, bilateral policy, submitted lineups and resource admission remain unchanged. No permanent provider store, new provider call, poller, large retained owner or background search is introduced.
+
+## Acceptance and limitations
+
+Controls use native disposable source publications, both one-QB/K/DEF and Superflex configurations, default and connected cache restoration, eviction/reopening, real Trade evaluation, authenticated rendered My Team/Market routes and explicit exact-target Trade For navigation. Browser measurements are Chromium keyboard/touch emulation, not physical iPhone/Safari.
+
+The owner's supplied Granite observation establishes its provisional state but not its particular cause. This session has no owner-authenticated browser or Render Shell capability. The unchanged external inspection binding's previous401 is not retried. Genuine unknown availability, eligible missing reserves, incomplete lineups, stale sources and failed refreshes still appropriately withhold personalized actions. Shipping this correction cannot establish live Granite recovery or prove that a player improves a legal lineup or that an offer would qualify.
+
+Final original local/hosted counts, source tree, resource samples, immutable release evidence and exact live limitations are recorded in the release handoff, without relabeling development controls as frozen-candidate acceptance.
